stm(3, `Hardy-Weinberg`, `Gene flow can make two populations more alike.`, `Genetic drift is stronger in large populations.`, 2, `Statement I is correct as migrants mix the gene pools. Statement II is wrong: drift is stronger in small populations.`);
stm(3, `origin of life`, `Miller\'s experiment formed amino acids from inorganic gases.`, `Miller\'s experiment formed living cells.`, 2, `I is correct; II is wrong. The result supports chemical evolution only.`);
stm(3, `human evolution`, `Homo habilis had a brain capacity of 650 to 800 cc.`, `Neanderthal man had a brain smaller than Homo erectus.`, 2, `I is correct. II is wrong as the Neanderthal had about 1400 cc and Homo erectus had about 900 cc.`);
