nat(4, `Hardy-Weinberg`, `In a population in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium, 1 in 400 people shows an autosomal recessive disease. In a town of 2000 people, about how many are expected to be carriers?`, 190, `q<sup>2</sup> = 1/400 = 0.0025, so q = 0.05 and p = 0.95. 2pq = 2 &times; 0.95 &times; 0.05 = 0.095. Carriers = 0.095 &times; 2000 = 190.`, ``, `Do not use q for carriers. The carrier frequency is 2pq.`);
nat(4, `Hardy-Weinberg`, `A population of 500 has 200 AA, 200 Aa and 100 aa individuals. If it were in Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium with the same allele frequencies, how many Aa individuals would be expected?`, 240, `Total alleles = 1000. A = 2 &times; 200 + 200 = 600, so p = 0.6 and q = 0.4. 2pq = 0.48, and 0.48 &times; 500 = 240. The actual number (200) is less, so it is not in equilibrium.`, ``, `Count alleles first, not genotypes.`);
