stm(4, `selection`, `Stabilising selection decreases the variance of a trait in the population.`, `Disruptive selection decreases the variance of a trait in the population.`, 2, `Stabilising selection removes extremes and narrows the curve, so the spread falls. Disruptive selection removes the middle and raises the spread. II is wrong.`);
stm(4, `Darwin`, `Natural selection acts on the phenotype of an individual.`, `Allele frequencies of the population change as a result.`, 0, `Selection acts on traits that are the phenotype. The proportion of the alleles behind the favoured trait rises in the next generation, so the gene pool changes.`);
